*> CC-0014 (bug wave round 4), the viewer's side of a goat horn in use (docs/protocol/58-in-use-item-models-and-arm-poses.md sections 2.3, 5.1, 5.3, 5.4 and 8.1): another player's entry 8
*> (Set Entity Data, bit 0 uses an item, bit 1 the off hand) with the Set Equipment of the used hand through the real packet path starts the viewer's use count (140 for a goat horn; 0 for a
*> horn whose patch removes the instrument component and for any other item; not restarted by a repeated entry 8; not started from an empty hand until a later entry 8 retries; cleared by a
*> clear flag; stopped when the used hand holds another item; counted down by ENTITIES-ANIM-TICK), and the arm that holds the horn gets the pose TOOT_HORN while the count is above 0: the arm frame
*> found when the player was drawn (EN-HAND-F) has the axes of the rotation (xRot -1.4835298, yRot -+0.5235988, zRot +-0.1 with the idle bob at age 0) that 58 section 8.1 gives for head pitch 0 and
*> yaw 0, the other arm its own pose. The axes are the unit axes of the document's arm angles worked by scratchpad/bwb-r5/ref_frame.py (the same chain that reproduces the ITEM and BLOCK frames
*> of test_entity_shield).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-ENTITY-USE-HORN.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY CONTENT.
 COPY CLMODELS.
