 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "PACK-STACK-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     ADD 1 TO PK-COUNT
     INITIALIZE PK-PACK(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE 1 TO PK-KIND(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE 3 TO PK-LEVEL(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE "generated/vanilla" TO PK-ID(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE 17 TO PK-ID-LENGTH(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE "client/tests/fixtures/mini-vanilla" TO PK-ROOT(PK-COUNT)
     MOVE 34 TO PK-ROOT-LENGTH(PK-COUNT)
     CALL "PACK-STACK-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "PACK-SOURCE-FILES" USING CLIENT-STATE PK-COUNT
     CALL "ATLAS-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "ENTITY-ATLAS-BUILD" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE CT-TYPE-STANDARD TO CT-SET-TYPE
     CALL "CONTENT-SET-COUNTS"
     MOVE 1 TO CT-OPEN
     MOVE 256 TO PL-HEIGHT
     MOVE 0 TO SK-U
     MOVE 10 TO WS-EYE(1) WS-EYE(3)
     MOVE 64 TO WS-EYE(2)
     MOVE 1 TO CL-CAMERA
     MOVE "goat_horn" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-HORN WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE "stick" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ITEM-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-STICK WS-ITEM-ROW WS-STATUS
     MOVE "player" TO WS-KEY
     CALL "CONTENT-ENTITY-BY-KEY" USING WS-KEY WS-TYPE WS-ROW-AREA WS-STATUS
     CALL "ENTITIES-CLEAR" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "UH-SPAWN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-TYPE WS-X WS-Y WS-Z WS-YAW
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
*>   Start: the horn in the main hand, then entry 8 with bit 0.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SLOT WS-REMOVE
     MOVE WS-HORN TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "UH-EQUIP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-ITEM WS-REMOVE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: entry 8 bit 0 with a horn in the main hand starts the use" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-ACTIVE(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: the used item is the horn" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-HORN TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-ITEM(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: the count of a horn starts at 140 (58 section 8.1)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 140 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-LEFT(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-AGE(1)
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FI WS-HNO
     MOVE "right arm raised with the horn (TOOT_HORN)" TO WS-CASE-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-FRAME
     MOVE 4 TO WS-FI
     MOVE 2 TO WS-HNO
     MOVE "left arm of the empty off hand" TO WS-CASE-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-FRAME
*>   The tick counts the use down; a repeated entry 8 does not restart it.
     PERFORM 3 TIMES
         CALL "ENTITIES-ANIM-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: three client ticks leave 137 and a repeated entry 8 does not restart the count" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 137 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-LEFT(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SLOT
     CALL "ENTITY-USING-HAND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-FLAG
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: using_item is true for the main hand's stack" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-FLAG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 2 TO WS-SLOT
     CALL "ENTITY-USING-HAND" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-FLAG
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: using_item is false for the off hand" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-FLAG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   The pose needs the count above 0: a spent count leaves the ITEM pose, whatever bit 0 says.
     MOVE 0 TO EN-USE-LEFT(1) EN-AGE(1)
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-FI
     MOVE 1 TO WS-HNO
     MOVE "right arm with a spent count (ITEM pose)" TO WS-CASE-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-FRAME
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: the pose test reads the count, not bit 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 5 TO EN-USE-LEFT(1)
     MOVE 0 TO EN-LIVING(1)
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SLOT
     CALL "ENTITY-HORN-POSE" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-FLAG
     MOVE WS-FLAG TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Clear: entry 8 without bit 0.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: a clear flag empties the use state" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-USE-ACTIVE(1) + EN-USE-ITEM(1) + EN-USE-LEFT(1)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   The off hand: the horn in the off hand, a stick in the main hand, flags 3.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SLOT
     MOVE WS-HORN TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "UH-EQUIP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-ITEM WS-REMOVE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SLOT
     MOVE WS-STICK TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "UH-EQUIP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-ITEM WS-REMOVE
     MOVE 3 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: entry 8 bits 0 and 1 start the use of the off hand's horn at 140" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 140 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-LEFT(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: the used item of the off hand is the horn" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE WS-HORN TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-ITEM(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-AGE(1)
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 3 TO WS-FI
     MOVE 2 TO WS-HNO
     MOVE "left arm raised with the horn (TOOT_HORN, mirrored yRot)" TO WS-CASE-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-FRAME
     MOVE 2 TO WS-FI
     MOVE 1 TO WS-HNO
     MOVE "right arm with the stick (ITEM pose)" TO WS-CASE-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-FRAME
*>   The stick replaces the horn in the used hand: the viewer's tick stops the use.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-SLOT
     MOVE WS-STICK TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "UH-EQUIP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-ITEM WS-REMOVE
     CALL "ENTITIES-ANIM-TICK" USING CLIENT-STATE
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: another item in the used hand stops the use at the next tick" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-USE-ACTIVE(1) + EN-USE-LEFT(1)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   Another item (the stick) in use: active, no count, no horn pose.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SLOT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: another item is in use with no count" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = EN-USE-ACTIVE(1) + EN-USE-LEFT(1)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   An empty hand at the start leaves the use unstarted; the next entry 8 retries it with the stack that arrived.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE 0 TO WS-SLOT
     MOVE 0 TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "UH-EQUIP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-ITEM WS-REMOVE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: bit 0 over an empty hand leaves the use unstarted" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-ACTIVE(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE WS-HORN TO WS-ITEM
     CALL "UH-EQUIP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-ITEM WS-REMOVE
     MOVE 5 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: a later entry 8 with bit 0 starts the count from the stack that arrived" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 140 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-LEFT(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
*>   A horn whose patch removes the instrument component (type 63) has a use duration of 0: in use, no count, and no pose.
     MOVE 0 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-REMOVE
     CALL "UH-EQUIP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-SLOT WS-ITEM WS-REMOVE
     MOVE 1 TO WS-FLAGS
     CALL "UH-DATA" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-ID WS-FLAGS
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: a horn without the instrument component is in use" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-ACTIVE(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "CC-0014 viewer: a horn without the instrument component has a count of 0" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE EN-USE-LEFT(1) TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE 0 TO EN-AGE(1)
     CALL "ENTITIES-MESH" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-EYE-TABLE
     MOVE 2 TO WS-FI
     MOVE 1 TO WS-HNO
     MOVE "right arm of a horn without an instrument (ITEM pose)" TO WS-CASE-NAME
     PERFORM CHECK-FRAME
     MOVE 0 TO CT-OPEN
     STOP RUN.

*> The arm frame of the row (EN-HAND-F: origin, then the three axes) of arm WS-HNO against frame WS-FI: the three axes as unit vectors, each component within 0.0005.
 CHECK-FRAME.
     MOVE 1 TO WS-OK
     PERFORM VARYING WS-A FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-A > 2
         COMPUTE WS-LEN = FUNCTION SQRT(EN-HAND-F(1, WS-HNO, 4 + WS-A * 3) ** 2 + EN-HAND-F(1, WS-HNO, 5 + WS-A * 3) ** 2
             + EN-HAND-F(1, WS-HNO, 6 + WS-A * 3) ** 2)
         PERFORM VARYING WS-K FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-K > 3
             COMPUTE WS-IDX = WS-A * 3 + WS-K
             IF WS-LEN = 0 OR FUNCTION ABS(EN-HAND-F(1, WS-HNO, 3 + WS-IDX) / WS-LEN - WS-FV(WS-FI, WS-IDX)) > 0.0005
                 MOVE 0 TO WS-OK
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-CASE
     STRING "CC-0014 viewer: " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-CASE-NAME) ": the arm frame's axes are the document's" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE WS-OK TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-ENTITY-USE-HORN.

